I just finished playing a Samurai who did rather well (and it is tough to
play a Lawful character for some of us ;), but I found what seems to be a
snag. I kill the Wizard (around ten times I imagine) but never found the
Book of the Dead (object detection didn't show it on the tower level he
died on, wading around the entire moat with an amulet of breathing didn't
show it, etc. I looked everywhere). I cleared pretty much everything else
out of the various dungeons, but no book, so no amulet. I'm not really too
ticked, because it takes too long to ascend anyway (carrying the amulet and
not being able to teleport is a pain), but I'm curious - what happened to
the book? Can the game screw up like this?

I even tried wishing for it (I had very few wishes in this game, but I only
really needed to wish for grey dragon mail - none of the grey dragons I
killed would leave me their hides), but it can't be done, even if you've
already killed the Wizard. Strange.

Near the end, the game seemed to be acting a bit stingy in other ways as
well - I killed 30 or 40 wraiths, and never saw a single corpse (so no
easy levels). The beehive in the Wizard's tower didn't yield any royal
jelly, either (though I'd found piles of it earlier).

Any ideas where the book could have gone? No-one stole it, and the Wizard
died on a dry-land space. I did kill him after throwing a potion of paralysis
at him, but I've done that before and still found the book.

Oh well, it was admittedly getting a bit dull anyway. Maybe I can say I've
got this silly game out of my system now.

